       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is about twice the labeled maximum daily dose. The US label maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas this a typo or a unit mix-up? Some options:\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **850 mg three times daily** (2,550 mg/day), the usual maximum for immediate-release.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg** per dose at a different frequency.\n\nTell me the intended dose and I'll enter it right away. If you really do need a dose above the labeled maximum, it needs to go through pharmacy or the attending's review, and I can't enter it on my own."
      }
