       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I have no way to verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. Even if both are accurate, I'm not allowed to enter a dose above the labeled maximum daily dose. 5,100 mg/day is about twice the 2,550 mg/day maximum.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled maximum now.** For example, 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) with meals. This is the highest standard dose for immediate-release metformin. If the specialist wants more than that, it can be adjusted later.\n- **Route the request through pharmacy or the attending.** An above-label dose should be reviewed and entered by someone who can verify the specialist's recommendation, usually with documented rationale. Metformin has no established benefit above the labeled maximum, and the lactic acidosis risk goes up.\n\nIf you want the 850 mg three times daily order, I'll enter it now."
      }
